{"verdict":"changes","notes":"`liveTrack.isCancelled` is checked separately from the final ledger append and the flow cleanup. A cancel can be accepted after that check but before append/cleanup, producing a successful row or deleting the worktree even though the socket returned success; cancellation accepted after `runPhase` can also allow subsequent checks, pushes, or merges to continue without a cancellation gate. The cancellation branch also preserves an existing non-nil `err` verbatim, so a cancelled early-failure row can omit the requested by/why reason. Finally, `preservedWorktrees` is only a process-global map: after a daemon restart it is empty and `reapOrphanWorktrees` removes the cancelled worktree, while the preservation test never exercises a new process or reset map. The live acceptance test reads `liveTrack.snapshot()` directly rather than querying status through the socket.","reviewer":"verifier","model":"openrouter/openai/gpt-5.6-luna","def_sha":"8531e5c611fd2ed2","run_id":"20260808T105824Z-branch-forest/163-serve-live-run-status-and-cancel","time":"2026-08-08T11:01:14Z"}
